 ### SnowPakTool Desktop UI
 
-The **Randomizer** main tab contains **Region progression** first, followed by **Truck-Randomization**. **Region progression** offers Easy, Normal, and Hard radio buttons and a Randomize button that automatically saves the suggested play order. It always starts in the easiest populated difficulty tier (D is easiest, S hardest), then uses a rising difficulty target with weighted variation; Hard favors tougher regions earlier. Unsorted regions go last when generating. The wrapping region tiles use the same soft background tints as the Region Difficulty tier panes (neutral gray for Unsorted) with contrasting text, and show larger, heavier circular position numbers in badges matching the header height, and read left to right then continue on the next row. They use the same drag preview and insertion marker as the tier lists; manual reordering saves automatically and renumbers the badges. Previous randomization restores one prior order kept in memory for this session. Finalize saves and locks the current order, disabling Randomize, Previous, difficulty controls, and tile moves; it becomes Unlock to allow changes again. The finalized state survives restarts. New regions append to the saved order without moving existing placements; tier and difficulty changes do not reroll the order. This uses all regions listed by the current workspace and does not modify game data. **Truck-Randomization** displays side-by-side Obtainable and Missions rule panes. The Obtainable pane starts with the six randomization rules (ownership, class, variety, progression, tires, and required addons); Missions starts empty. Each pane has a compact + glyph to add a rule; every rule has pencil and trash glyphs to edit and remove it. Tooltips identify each action. Edits save automatically between sessions; empty lists stay empty. The Obtainable pane can randomize owned obtainable placements after Region progression is finalized. It uses ranked owned trucks from the same app class, a progression-weighted truck tier draw, a repetition penalty, difficulty-weighted tire categories, and the smallest supported tire size/first variant. Required listed addons are preserved through compatible equivalents (including sideboard capacity); incompatible trucks are rejected and another candidate is tried. Unranked regions/trucks, unverified placements, missions, and unavailable configurations are not guessed. Saved assignments remain fixed across restarts and ownership changes. This pane shows region completion/error messages without revealing choices. Show detailed logs is off by default; enabling it reveals recorded placement messages in their original order, including tire-category variation, compatibility fallbacks, and rejected candidates, without naming replacement trucks. Actual trucks and equipment are shown in Game data → Regions-Trucks. That tab has Reset truck to original and Reset selected regions to original buttons, which clear assignments and queue restoration of the original model and exact map equipment. You can rerandomize a reset preview immediately, without applying the restoration first. Start → Apply map changes performs all map writes, carrying the chosen tires/addons through preview and Apply. Start also hides randomized replacement details so applying does not spoil the result. Old manual pending-change arrays are read and upgraded atomically when saved. Mission randomization is not configured. Editable rule text remains descriptive notes; editing prose does not change the implemented constraints.
